        "system": {
          "apparelType": "armor",
          "attachable": true,
          "attached": false,
          "canBeScrapped": true,
          "cost": 15,
          "description": "<h2><span class=\"fontstyle0\">Shadowed Armor</span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Many of the armor types listed in this section can be modified to become&nbsp;</span><span class=\"fontstyle3\">Shadowed</span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">. Shadowed armor has a darker, less-reflective surface to make it harder to see the wearer in dim light or darkness.</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"fontstyle2\">If you are wearing one or two pieces of Shadowed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">armor, you may ignore the first complication rolled on a </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\"><strong>Sneak</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">test you attempt while in dim light or darkness.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontstyle2\">If you are wearing three or more pieces of Shadowed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">armor, you may re-roll a single d20 on one </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\"><strong>Sneak</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">test </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">you attempt each scene while in dim light or darkness.</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"fontstyle2\">If you are wearing five or more pieces of Shadowed </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">armor, you may re-roll a single d20 on any </span><span class=\"fontstyle3\"><strong>Sneak</strong> </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">test </span><span class=\"fontstyle2\">you attempt while in dim light or darkness.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span class=\"fontstyle2\">Torso armor counts as two pieces towards this. Shadowed armor does not provide any bonus if you are in a suit of Power Armor.</span> <br><br></p>",
